    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Dragon Breath",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The chimera breathes a cone or line that deals 9d6 damage to all creatures in the area (DC 26 basic save of a type indicated below). The chimera's dragon head is linked to one of the traditions of magic, which determines the area of its Dragon Breath, the type of damage it deals, and the type of save to avoid it. This ability gains the related traits.\n\nThe chimera can't use Dragon Breath again for 1d4 rounds.\n\n- Arcane 60-foot line of force (DC 26 basic Reflex save)\n\n- Divine 60-foot line of spirit (DC 26 basic Reflex save); this ability can also have the holy or unholy trait\n\n- Occult 30-foot cone of mental (DC 26 basic Will save)\n\n- Primal 30-foot cone of acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic (DC 26 basic Reflex save); or poison (DC 26 basic Fortitude save)",
